# Managed by home/srvs/claude-memory.nix; edits here are overwritten.
#
# Union-merge every memory file. When both machines edit the same memory (very
# likely for MEMORY.md, the index that gains a line per new memory), git keeps
# BOTH sides' lines rather than raising a conflict. Duplicated text in a memory
# file is trivial to clean up; a memory silently lost to a botched conflict
# resolution is not — and an unresolvable conflict would wedge the sync for
# every other memory too. Union is the right trade here.
*.md merge=union
